\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Multi-head, grouped-query, and compressed-attention variants}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{attention}

\p{The multi-head construction in \ref{ftip-000U} stores a key and value
projection per query head. Grouped-query attention instead partitions query heads into groups that share key and
value heads; see Ainslie et al., Section 2
\citelink{https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13245}. This changes parameter and cache
shapes while preserving the query-key-value semantics.}

\p{Multi-head latent attention first compresses key-value information through
a lower-dimensional latent representation and reconstructs head-specific
quantities; see DeepSeek-V2, Section 2.1
\citelink{https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.04434}. DeepSeek-V3, Section 2.1, records a
later use of that architecture
\citelink{https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.19437}. These architectural differences
do not establish that their post-training effects equal those of ordinary
multi-head attention.}
